      <body>
         <entry xml:id="tibiqon-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">תיביקון</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">tybyqwn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">tibiqon</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">adjective</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="tibiqon-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>Thebaic cubit</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>θηβαϊκός</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>וזה אשר תעשה אותה. אמר ר' יודן זה וזה עתיד אחד למוד באמתך. הה"ד ארך הביינין במידה הראשונה אמות עשרים ורחב אמות עשרים. ולמה הוא קורא אותה 
                     <app>
                        <lem>תייביקון</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">תיבייקין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">תוביקון</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V Ox2">אמה תביקין</rdg>
                     </app> ר' הונא אמר שהיא מתביאית, ורבנין אמ' על שם תיבתו שלנח</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">31, 10</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 282: 5</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>And this is how thou shalt make it (Gen 6,15). R. Yudan said: And this [is written where] this [would have sufficed]: [God intimated]: Another is destined to measure with thy cubit, as it is written, The length of the building after the ancient [lit. ‘first’] measure was twenty cubits, and the breadth twenty cubits (2 Chr 3,3). And why is it [the cubit] called tibiqon? R. Huna said: Because it comes from Thebes. The Rabbis said: On account of Noah’s tevah (ark). (Freedman / Simon I 243)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 53 [I 177: 4]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">תביקון</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Cf. <bibl type="modern">MY ad loc</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">AC VIII 200ab</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Levy IV 625a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Fürst (1890) 212a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Zuckermann (1867) 21</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Jastrow II 1643a</bibl>. Krauss, LW II suggests also <term xml:lang="jpa">קוביקון</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">qwbyqwn</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">qubikon</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">κυβικόν</term>.</note>
